{
 "text": "Say you've got a C-I-D, and you've found some server you've never heard of that claims to have it. You ask, and bytes start flowing back.\n\nIn the last episode, the advice was \"always verify.\" That sounds simple, and it mostly is. But it's worth getting precise about, because there are a few small decisions that separate a check that's airtight from one that only looks airtight. And once verification is solid, it unlocks something very nice: permission to cache forever.",
